/BINARY INTERCHANGE PROGRAM
/
/	BBBBBBB		   IIIII		PPPPPPP
/	B      B	     I			P      P
/	B      B	     I			P      P
/	B      B	     I			P      P
/	BBBBBBB		     I   		PPPPPPP
/	B      B	     I			P
/	B      B	     I			P
/	B      B	     I			P
/	BBBBBBB		   IIIII		P
/
/NEW IMPROVED P?S BINARY LOADER
/DEFAULT ADDRESS 7777
/USED IF NO STARTING ADDRESS PASSED
/SETTING SWITCHES 0 THROUGH 7 SPECIFIES WHICH FIELD TO START IN
/IF MORE THAN ONE FIELD SPECIFIED,LOWEST FIELD PASSED WILL BE USED
/PASSED OUTPUT FILES ARE CHECKED FOR AND THEN IGNORED
/MAXIMUM NUMBER OF BINARY INPUT FILES = 7 FROM UNITS 0 AND 1
/ANY FURTHER FILES ARE IGNORED
/TYPICAL USAGES:
/RUN BIN,BFILE1,BFILE2,BFILE3,BFILE4,BFILE5,BFILE6,BFILE7
/LOADS 7 FILES,STARTS AT 7640 (HALTS) IN FIELD 0
/RUN BIN<FILE1,FILE2=200
/LOADS 2 FILES AND THEN STARTS AT 200 FIELD 0
/RUN BIN,DUM1,DUM2<FILE1
/LOADS ONLY ONE FILE (FILE1) AND THEN HALTS
/RUN BIN,FILE1/1
/THIS WILL HALT BECAUSE NO STARTING ADDRESS PASSED,EVEN IF FIELD SWITCH SET
/RUN BIN=200
/LOADS DEFAULT ("$") FILE,(BLOCKS 20-37)STARTING AT 200
/THE FIRST FILE PASSED ,IF IT IS DOLLAR REFERS TO THE SPECIAL BINARY FILE
/KNOWN AS THE BIN.ANY FURTHER FILES REFER TO THE TRANSIENT FILE FOUND
/AT THE BEGINNING OF EACH TAPE (BLOCKS 40-57)
/RUN BIN,$,$=200
/LOADS 2 FILES THE BIN(20-37) AND DOLLOR(40-57)
/AND STARTS AT LOCATION 200 IN FIELD 0 WHEN DONE.
/THIS APPLIES TO UNIT 1 AS WELL.
/RUN BIN,BFILE/1=200/H/AFTER FILLING MOST OF CORE WITH HLTS (7402)
/LOADS FILE BFILE STARTING AT LOCATION 200 IN FIELD 1
	PAGE
